-- title:
--   Equation (1.5) — Relative-entropy regularization as a normalized block limit
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ and $B$ be nonzero finite-dimensional complex Hilbert spaces, and let $N,M:\mathcal L(A)\to\mathcal L(B)$ be completely positive, trace-preserving maps. For each positive integer $n$, let $D(N^{\otimes n}\Vert M^{\otimes n})$ be the stabilized channel relative entropy in bits, optimized over normalized pure inputs with a reference copy of $A^{\otimes n}$.
--
--   Define
--
--   $$
--   D^{\mathrm{reg}}(N\Vert M)
--   =\sup_{n\ge1}\frac{D(N^{\otimes n}\Vert M^{\otimes n})}{n}.
--   $$
--
--   Then
--
--   $$
--   \lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{D(N^{\otimes n}\Vert M^{\otimes n})}{n}
--   =D^{\mathrm{reg}}(N\Vert M).
--   $$
--
--   The identity holds in $[0,+\infty]$ without a support or finiteness assumption. Inputs may be entangled across all $n$ uses. This establishes the relative-entropy instance of the paper's regularization identity and connects its asymptotic definition with the formal positive-block supremum.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The totalized block value at zero is excluded from the defining supremum and does not affect convergence as the block length tends to infinity.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/JWang226/Continuity-of-regularized-channel-renyi-divergence/blob/e29274a69978bb499f00497481c6008befb0b84d/QuantumChannelContinuity/RegularizationLimits.lean#L125-L130

